{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. Thompson. I'm Dr. Patel, one of your hospital doctors. You're here today for your scheduled chemotherapy cycle, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. Cycle 33 of methotrexate. I’ve been doing this for a while now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s impressive consistency. How have you been feeling at home lately?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:06:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pretty well, actually. No pain, no fevers, no shortness of breath. My last urology visit went smoothly—stent was removed and I haven’t had any issues since."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. I see you had a recent admission for kidney stones. Good that it’s resolved. Any nausea, diarrhea, or rashes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:09:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing like that. Just the usual tiredness sometimes, but I expected that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:10:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Understood. We’ll keep an eye on your energy levels. Let me check your vitals quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure is 104 over 64, heart rate 66, temperature normal, oxygen level 95% on room air. All stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. My blood pressure’s usually a bit low, but I don’t feel dizzy or anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "As long as you’re not symptomatic, it’s fine. Now, I see in your list you’re still taking lisinopril. Wasn’t that stopped during your last admission?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, really? I didn’t realize. I just kept taking it. Should I stop?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll review it with neuro-oncology, but likely yes, since your kidney function was affected last time. We’ll monitor your labs closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2188-10-24 11:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, makes sense. I don’t want to risk another kidney issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2188-10-24 12:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We just got your chest X-ray back. It shows your port is in good position, no fluid in the lungs or heart strain. Just some old scarring, unchanged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2188-10-24 12:52:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I was a bit worried about the port, but glad it’s okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2188-10-24 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs came back. White count and hemoglobin are stable. Sodium is a bit low at 128, but not as concerning as last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2188-10-24 14:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that because of the desmopressin again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2188-10-24 14:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll keep an eye on it. You’re on the nasal spray twice daily—still the same dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2188-10-24 14:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, one spray in the morning and one at night. My urine output seems normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2188-10-24 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll continue monitoring. Your kidney function is stable—creatinine is 1.0, which is within your baseline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2188-10-24 14:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Last time it went up, I was really worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2188-10-24 14:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll be cautious. Now, tomorrow you’ll get your chemotherapy—methotrexate, temozolomide, and we’ll start leucovorin and sodium bicarbonate to protect your kidneys and help clear the drug."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2188-10-24 14:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that routine. The sodium bicarbonate helps with the methotrexate clearance, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2188-10-24 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll give it intravenously at first, then switch you to oral tablets once your levels start to drop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2188-10-24 14:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And we’ll check my methotrexate levels daily?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2188-10-24 14:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll draw blood every morning. We want to see it drop below 0.2 before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2188-10-24 14:13:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll make sure to drink plenty of fluids too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2188-10-25 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re about to start the methotrexate infusion through your port. You’ll also get temozolomide by mouth, and we’ve started IV sodium bicarbonate and leucovorin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2188-10-25 12:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. Any side effects I should watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2188-10-25 12:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most common is mild nausea. We’ve given you anti-nausea meds just in case. Let us know if you feel any unusual fatigue, mouth sores, or rash."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2188-10-25 12:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had nausea before, but it usually passes in a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2188-10-25 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you comfortable. The infusion will take a few hours. Rest as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2188-10-26 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning labs are back. Your methotrexate level dropped from 3.76 last night to 0.20 this morning—great clearance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2188-10-26 06:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news! Does that mean I’m on track to go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2188-10-26 06:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if it stays below 0.2, we can discharge tomorrow. We’ll check one more level in the morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2188-10-26 06:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll still need the oral sodium bicarbonate?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2188-10-26 06:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, neuro-oncology wants you to continue it at home until your next appointment, since your level was still just above 0.1."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2188-10-26 06:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll take it as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2188-10-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat methotrexate level is 0.12—still dropping. We’re on track for discharge tomorrow afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2188-10-26 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Should I restart any medications I stopped?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2188-10-26 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We reviewed your lisinopril. Since your kidney function is stable, we’ll restart it at the same dose—5 mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2188-10-26 10:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good to know. And desmopressin—I’ll keep that as is?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2188-10-26 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue the nasal spray twice daily. Just monitor your urine output and avoid excessive fluid intake."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2188-10-26 10:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Any restrictions on activity?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2188-10-26 10:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can resume normal activities. Just listen to your body. If you feel unusually tired, rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2188-10-27 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final methotrexate level is 0.12—still acceptable for discharge. Your labs are stable, and you’ve tolerated everything well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2188-10-27 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2188-10-27 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll discharge you around 4 PM today. You’ll take home sodium bicarbonate, continue all your usual meds, and follow up with neuro-oncology in four months."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2188-10-27 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I feel unwell before then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2188-10-27 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your oncology team. Watch for fever, severe nausea, or confusion. Otherwise, you’re doing very well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2188-10-27 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2188-10-27 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you at your next cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2188-10-27 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check-in. Still feeling well?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2188-10-27 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, no issues. Just ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2188-10-27 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re finalizing your discharge paperwork. Pharmacy will send your prescriptions ahead."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2188-10-27 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your discharge orders are in. You’ll take sodium bicarbonate four times a day for now, and all your other meds as listed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2188-10-27 12:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll review them when I get home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2188-10-27 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nursing will go over your instructions one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2188-10-27 14:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I feel confident about managing things at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2188-10-27 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. Discharge is official. Take care, and we’ll see you in four months."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2188-10-27 16:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2188-10-27 16:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2188-10-27 16:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it. See you next time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2188-10-27 16:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. Thompson."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2188-10-27 16:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2188-10-27 16:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a smooth recovery at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2188-10-27 16:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I will."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2188-10-24 11:03:00",
    "admission_end": "2188-10-27 16:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 65-year-old man with a history of CNS diffuse large B-cell lymphoma was admitted for Cycle 33 of scheduled methotrexate chemotherapy. He reported feeling well since his recent outpatient ureteral stent removal and denied fevers, shortness of breath, nausea, or rashes. His hospital course was uncomplicated; he received methotrexate and temozolomide with leucovorin and sodium bicarbonate per protocol, tolerating treatment with only mild nausea. Methotrexate levels decreased appropriately, falling to 0.12 by discharge. His sodium was mildly low at 128 but stable, and creatinine remained normal at 1.0. Lisinopril, which had been held during a prior admission, was restarted given stable renal function. He was discharged home on oral sodium bicarbonate to continue until his next oncology visit in four months, with all other medications resumed as before. Follow-up was scheduled with neuro-oncology.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Diabetes insipidus",
      "Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Calculus of kidney",
      "Personal history of nicotine dependence",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Presence of artificial hip joint, bilateral"
    ]
  }
}
